# Copy this file to .env and fill in values ONLY when a lesson asks for them.
# Never commit .env — it is listed in .gitignore. Never paste a key into a notebook cell either:
# it would be saved with the notebook's outputs.
#
# Days 01-05 need no environment variables and no API keys. Day 04 downloads a small open
# embedding model once; these two OPTIONAL settings only matter on restricted networks:
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.com:8080   # your organisation's proxy
# HF_ENDPOINT=https://hf-mirror.example.com   # a Hugging Face mirror, if huggingface.co is blocked
#
# Day 06 (OPTIONAL): a real language model for the generation step. Leave these commented out to use
# the API-free reader, which is the default and needs nothing. The Day 06 notebook reads the RAG_CHAT_*
# settings only from this .env file, and calls a model only when you switch LIVE_MODEL on (section 8.2).
# Uncomment ONE option:
#
# Option A: Ollama, local and free (https://docs.ollama.com). Install it, pull a small instruction-tuned
# chat model, and put that model's name here. Nothing leaves your computer; no key needed.
# RAG_CHAT_PROVIDER=ollama
# RAG_CHAT_MODEL=your-pulled-model
#
# Option B: OpenAI, hosted, billed per token. gpt-6-luna cost USD 0.10 per million input tokens and
# USD 0.50 per million output tokens on 2026-10-20 (standard tier); the notebook's eight live questions
# cost at most about USD 0.0044. Your questions and the retrieved text are sent to OpenAI.
# RAG_CHAT_PROVIDER=openai
# RAG_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# RAG_CHAT_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# Optional with either: another OpenAI-compatible server (LM Studio, vLLM, a company gateway).
# RAG_CHAT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
